{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.checkWithKernel\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">checkWithKernel</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Throw an exception if `e` cannot be type checked using the kernel.\nThis function is used for debugging purposes only.\nBe sure to share common expressions in `e` before calling this function for good performance.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.checkWithKernel","kind":"def","line":377,"name":"Lean.Meta.checkWithKernel","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Check.lean#L377-L386"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.isTypeCorrect\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">isTypeCorrect</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Return true if `e` is type correct.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.isTypeCorrect","kind":"def","line":367,"name":"Lean.Meta.isTypeCorrect","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Check.lean#L367-L375"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.withInstancesTypeCheckNote\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">withInstancesTypeCheckNote</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> → <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a> u_1</span>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Control/Basic.html#MonadControlT\">MonadControlT</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span></span>]</span></span> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">[<span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Monad\">Monad</a> <span class=\"fn\">m</span></span>]</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">x</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">m</span> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Runs `x` and, on any error, lazily checks whether `e` is type-correct at `instances` transparency.\nIf not, appends an explanatory note to the error message.\n\nThis is useful for tactics like `rw` and `simp` whose failure modes can be caused by\nprior tactics (such as `unfold`) leaving the goal in a state that's type-correct only at\n`.default` transparency, preventing unification etc at `.instances`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.withInstancesTypeCheckNote","kind":"def","line":345,"name":"Lean.Meta.withInstancesTypeCheckNote","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Check.lean#L345-L365"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.check\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">check</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">transparency</span> : <a href=\"./Init/MetaTypes.html#Lean.Meta.TransparencyMode\">TransparencyMode</a> := <a href=\"./Init/MetaTypes.html#Lean.Meta.TransparencyMode.all\">TransparencyMode.all</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Throw an exception if `e` is not type correct at the given transparency.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.check","kind":"def","line":333,"name":"Lean.Meta.check","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Check.lean#L333-L343"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.checkProj\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">checkProj</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">structName</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Lean.Name\">Name</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">idx</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">e</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.checkProj","kind":"def","line":287,"name":"Lean.Meta.checkProj","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Check.lean#L287-L291"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.checkApp\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">checkApp</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f </span><span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Unit\">Unit</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.checkApp","kind":"def","line":277,"name":"Lean.Meta.checkApp","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Check.lean#L277-L285"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.throwAppTypeMismatch\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">throwAppTypeMismatch</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">f </span><span class=\"fn\">a</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.throwAppTypeMismatch","kind":"def","line":255,"name":"Lean.Meta.throwAppTypeMismatch","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Check.lean#L255-L275"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.mkHasTypeButIsExpectedMsg\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkHasTypeButIsExpectedMsg</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">givenType </span><span class=\"fn\">expectedType</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">trailing?</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Message.html#Lean.MessageData\">MessageData</a></span> := <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option.none\">none</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">trailingExprs</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a></span> := <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List.toArray\">#[</a><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#List.toArray\">]</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Message.html#Lean.MessageData\">MessageData</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Return error message \"has type{givenType}\\nbut is expected to have type{expectedType}\"\nAdds the type’s types unless they are defeq.\n\nIf `trailing?` is non-`none`, it is appended to the end of the message. This requires modifying the\nproduced message, so prefer specifying `trailing?` over appending a message to the result of this\nfunction. Any expressions appearing in the trailing message should be included in `trailingExprs`.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.mkHasTypeButIsExpectedMsg","kind":"def","line":219,"name":"Lean.Meta.mkHasTypeButIsExpectedMsg","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Check.lean#L219-L253"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.mkUnfoldAxiomsNote\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">mkUnfoldAxiomsNote</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">givenType </span><span class=\"fn\">expectedType</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Message.html#Lean.MessageData\">MessageData</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Adds note about definitions not unfolded because of the module system, if any.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.mkUnfoldAxiomsNote","kind":"def","line":201,"name":"Lean.Meta.mkUnfoldAxiomsNote","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Check.lean#L201-L217"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.throwLetTypeMismatchMessage\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">throwLetTypeMismatchMessage</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">α</span> : <a href=\"./foundational_types.html\">Type</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">fvarId</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.FVarId\">FVarId</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> <span class=\"fn\">α</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.throwLetTypeMismatchMessage","kind":"def","line":191,"name":"Lean.Meta.throwLetTypeMismatchMessage","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Check.lean#L191-L199"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.addPPExplicitToExposeDiff\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">Meta</span>.<span class=\"name\">addPPExplicitToExposeDiff</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">b</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Meta/Basic.html#Lean.Meta.MetaM\">MetaM</a> (<a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Lean/Expr.html#Lean.Expr\">Expr</a>)</span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Given two expressions `a` and `b`, this method tries to annotate terms with `pp.explicit := true`\nand other `pp` options to expose \"implicit\" differences.\nFor example, suppose `a` and `b` are of the form\n```lean\n@HashMap Nat Nat eqInst hasInst1\n@HashMap Nat Nat eqInst hasInst2\n```\nBy default, the pretty printer formats both of them as `HashMap Nat Nat`.\nSo, counterintuitive error messages such as\n```lean\nerror: application type mismatch\n  HashMap.insert m\nargument\n  m\nhas type\n  HashMap Nat Nat\nbut is expected to have type\n  HashMap Nat Nat\n```\nwould be produced.\nBy adding `pp.explicit := true`, we can generate the more informative error\n```lean\nerror: application type mismatch\n  HashMap.insert m\nargument\n  m\nhas type\n  @HashMap Nat Nat eqInst hasInst1\nbut is expected to have type\n  @HashMap Nat Nat eqInst hasInst2\n```\n\nRemark: this method implements simple heuristics; we should extend it as we find other counterintuitive\nerror messages.","docLink":"./Lean/Meta/Check.html#Lean.Meta.addPPExplicitToExposeDiff","kind":"def","line":37,"name":"Lean.Meta.addPPExplicitToExposeDiff","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/c9afcddf514a6772bd4d649f7cfc04eff0b9f15e/src/Lean/Meta/Check.lean#L37-L189"}}],"imports":["Init.Data.Range.Polymorphic.Iterators","Lean.Meta.Sorry","Lean.OriginalConstKind"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Meta.Check"}